export PP_RBMODE=0
export PP_CORE_PLL=50M
export PP_INT_PLL=50M

The core PLL is the clock for the FPGA streamer circuit (decoder). The internal PLL generates the clock
for clocking out the data from the output FIFO buffer, i.e. it is the "data clock."

pptest 2 -int_clk -int_pll 25M -veryverbose -check
pptest 2 -ext_clk -veryverbose -check
pptest 2 -clk 2 -veryverbose -check

NOTE: FPGA reset is performed only if the clock source is changed (using `-int_clk`, `-ext_clk`, `-clk`, or the `PP_INT_CLK` / `PP_EXT_CLK` environment variables).
